### Economization of Series

_Problem: Given \(f(x)=\sum\limits_{m=0}^{n}a_{n}x^{m}\) in the interval \(-1\leq x\leq 1\) and \(R>0\). Find \(\widetilde{J}(x)=\sum\limits_{m=0}^{N}b_{m}x^{m}\) with \(N\) as small as possible, such that \(|\widetilde{J}(x)-\widetilde{J}(x)|<R\)._

_Solution: Express \(f(x)\) in terms of Chebyshev polynomials using Table 22.3,_

\[f(x) = \sum\limits_{m=0}^{n}b_{n}T_{m}(x)\]
